.TH "IDBRECORD" "3JS" "July 6, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
IDBRecord \- IDBRecord
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]IDBRecord\f[B]\f[R] interface of the IndexedDB API
represents a snapshot of a single record in an \f[CR]IDBObjectStore\f[R]
or \f[CR]IDBIndex\f[R].
.PP
A request for records using \f[CR]IDBObjectStore.getAllRecords()\f[R] or
\f[CR]IDBIndex.getAllRecords()\f[R] returns an \f[CR]IDBRequest\f[R]
instance.
On success, the returned object\(cqs \f[CR]result\f[R] property is
populated with an array of \f[CR]IDBRecord\f[R] instances.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]key\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
A value representing the record\(cqs secondary key.
For an object store record, this will be the same as
\f[CR]primaryKey\f[R].
For an index record, it will be the record\(cqs key within the index.
.TP
\f[B]primaryKey\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
A value representing the record\(cqs primary key.
This key is used to represent the record in the
\f[CR]IDBObjectStore\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]value\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
A value representing the record\(cqs value.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]None.\f[R]
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example queries an \f[CR]IDBObjectStore\f[R] for up to 100 records
whose keys come after \f[CR]\(dqmyKey\(dq\f[R], with results sorted in
reverse order.
.PP
The code first creates a transaction on an \f[CR]IDBDatabase\f[R] named
\f[CR]db\f[R] (omitting the code to open the database), and then uses it
to get an \f[CR]IDBObjectStore\f[R] containing a contacts list.
It then calls \f[CR]getAllRecords()\f[R] on the object store, returning
a \f[CR]IDBRequest\f[R] instance.
Event listeners are added to this request for the \f[CR]success\f[R] and
\f[CR]error\f[R] events.
On success, the result \f[CR]event.target.result\f[R] is logged (this is
also available as \f[CR]request.result\f[R]).
This result contains an array of \f[CR]IDBRecord\f[R] instances.
Note that because this is a query on an \f[CR]IDBObjectStore\f[R], the
\f[CR]key\f[R] and \f[CR]primaryKey\f[R] in each record have the same
value.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Create a transaction on the database and use it to get the contained store\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] transaction = db.transaction([\(dqcontactsList\(dq], \(dqreadonly\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] objectStore = transaction.objectStore(\(dqcontactsList\(dq);

\f[B]const\f[R] query = IDBKeyRange.lowerBound(\(dqmyKey\(dq, \f[B]true\f[R]);

\f[B]const\f[R] request = objectStore.getAllRecords({
  query,
  count: 100,
  direction: \(dqprev\(dq,
});

request.addEventListener(\(dqsuccess\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] myRecords = event.target.result; \f[I]// Array of IDBRecord instances\f[R]
  console.log(myRecords);
});

request.addEventListener(\(dqerror\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.error(\(dqError retrieving records:\(dq, event.target.error);
});
.EE
